  "english": "Midday Liturgy Office Hour [Introit]: Who shone upon us.\nHymn Tone 8 [dk]: Christ God. Psalm 44 [45]: She shall be brought to the king. Proverbs 31:29: Many daughters, to verse 31: forever.\nProphet Isaiah 61:10: My soul shall rejoice, to 62:3: of your God. Apostle Romans 15:30: I appeal to you, to 16:2: indeed completely. Alleluia: The queen shall stand. Gospel Matthew 10:26: For there is nothing, [to 10:33]: which is in heaven.\nIn the Evening Messedi: Of the Martyrs in the tone of the day. Hambartsi Tone 8 [dk]: Word without beginning. Litany: For peace. Prayer: Compassionate Father. Antiphon: He that dwelleth. Supplication: The Most High. Litany: And we in unison. Prayer: Hope of life. Our Father. And then Peace Service: without fail.\n\nTuesday. Tone 3 [b3]: Of the Holy Virgins Gaiane and her companions. In the Evening, perform the Pre-festive service [Nakhatonak]: Souls [Anzink] with its proper hymns. Likewise also in the night, sing the canon-blessing [Ah.], the Patrum [Harsh], the Magnificat [Mkk.], and the Hambartsi [Hmb.] of Saint Hripsime and her companions. Morning song: They shall boast. Midday Liturgy Office Hour [Introit]: The victorious. Hymn Tone 7 [dz]: Christ God. Psalm 44 [45]: She shall be brought. Proverbs 1:20: Wisdom, to verse 23: of reproof. Prophet Jeremiah (Baruch) 4:36: Look, to 5:4: of godliness. Apostle 2 Corinthians 6:16: For you are, to 7:1: with fear of God. Alleluia: The queen shall stand. Gospel John 16:1: These things I have spoken, to verse 5: because I was with you.\n\nKeep the order of the Patrum [Harsh] of Repentance in this manner.\nStarting from this Wednesday, on all Wednesdays and fast days of the week on which there are no feasts,\nsay in order all the Patrum [Harsh] of Repentance except for two, Tone 2 [bk] and Tone 8 [dk] composition; that is, except for the Patrum [Harsh] \"God powerful\" and \"Your name forever.\"\nAnd upon finishing them, begin again to say only the fast [alts] hymns until you reach the Sunday of Saint Sarkis; the Directory also shows you this. And\nas for the canon-blessings [Orh.] of such fasts and of Fridays, say the Repentance Miserere [Oghormya] in the tone of the day.\nLikewise also in the evenings: say the Messedi and the Hambartsi of Repentance in the tone of the day.\nWednesday. Tone 4 [bk]. Patrum [Harsh]: God, Who lookest with sweetness. Morning song: I...",
